From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:37:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 20/26] Safarium: native Settings window
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Safarium > Settings… (⌘,) opens a native, Safari-style settings window
(NSTabViewController, toolbar style) instead of the chrome://settings
tab. Panes:
- General: startup (new tab / last session), Home button and the page
  it opens, download folder and "ask where to save", default browser.
- Tabs: compact or vertical layout, tab previews and their memory
  usage, always show the toolbar in full screen.
- AutoFill: passwords, auto sign-in, addresses, cards, each with Edit…
  into the existing pages.
- Advanced: website data, extensions, and Show All Settings… for
  chrome://settings.
Each control reads and writes the same pref chrome://settings uses,
follows changes made elsewhere, and is disabled when a policy sets it.
The last pane is remembered. One window per profile; it closes when its
profile goes away.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
